## Key Architectural Notes

> [!WARNING]
> **No real database** — All admin changes are stored in `localStorage`, meaning:
> - Data is per-browser and per-device only
> - Clearing browser data wipes all admin edits
> - Changes don't sync across users or devices

> [!NOTE]
> **No API routes** — The project has no `app/api/` directory. Everything is client-side rendered or statically generated.

> [!TIP]
> To add persistent data storage, you would need to integrate a backend database (e.g., Supabase, Firebase, or a custom API) and replace the `localStorage`-based data service.
